 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It' an effect of thin layers of paint on top of each other. A light layer of white first, then the Dark on top? shot of it with good light before you go? The room it' in change how the painting looks by ten percent. Take a good flash with a few different cameras, they give the odd patterns. Also a cell phone in a lockbox. Going from bright room to darkness turns every gloss into a neon line. A soft dunt with a finger or two of erasable marker first, then the gloss seal if you want it glossy.",
